    "status": "present",
    "value": "Tokenise by padding parentheses with spaces. Walk the tokens once, keeping a stack of frames, one per open form, recording the operator, operand values, a pending variable name for let, the names it bound, and its body value. Each completed value (a literal, a variable lookup or a closed form) is delivered to the frame on top: add/mult collect it as an operand; let either binds it to the pending name or takes it as the body. Shadowing is handled by a map from name to a stack of values: binding pushes, and closing a let pops each name it bound. Lookup reads the top of that name's stack."
  },
